description:
We are looking for an Executive Officer to join the Faculty of Dentistry to provide comprehensive administrative support for undergraduate programme management.

The appointee will play a key role in managing and supporting undergraduate programme administration, including but not limited to:

Programme and curriculum planning, administration and revision;

Academic reviews, accreditation exercises and quality assurance processes;

Development, planning and coordination of new undergraduate programmes and articulation programmes;

Planning and support of student enrichment and wellness activities;

A Bachelor’s degree with at least 3 years’ administrative experience, preferably in tertiary education institutions;

Strong organisational, communication, analytical and problem-solving skills;

Meticulous attention to details, strong self-motivation and ability to work both independently and collaboratively;

An excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua);

Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and other relevant computer softwares; and

Experiences in undergraduate programme administration and academic reviews are preferred.

Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 534046) need not re-apply.

The appointment will be made on a fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years and commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits.

The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University's careers site (https://jobs.hku.hk) and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until April 15, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview.

